{"h":3395,"w":2400,"lines":[{"t":"Test 5","c":1,"w":0.061728394826253266,"h":0.013081395583944722,"x":0.10082304528234663,"y":0.071220930091644763},{"w":0.50205759684244788,"c":1,"y":0.11627907012247718,"h":0.021824581743831173,"x":0.26748972009931188,"t":"What's the purpose of gaining knowledge?"},{"t":"'I would found an institution where any person can find instruction in any","x":0.1460905366918443,"w":0.67283950805664072,"y":0.15547703145642833,"c":1,"h":0.018941572613935143},{"t":"subject.' That was the founder's motto for Cornell University, and it seems an apt","c":1,"x":0.14609053360603658,"w":0.73045267740885422,"y":0.17432273212654725,"h":0.018991220966244837},{"h":0.019140164899882128,"t":"characterization of the different university, also in the USA, where I currently teach","x":0.14609055570203974,"y":0.19316843350228075,"w":0.74691355387369773,"c":1},{"t":"philosophy. A student can prepare for a carcer in resort management, engineering,","x":0.1479956682114249,"h":0.021860228270046522,"c":1,"y":0.21219292736347517,"w":0.73687184651692705},{"h":0.021872216034834135,"c":1,"y":0.23077394113792693,"w":0.7430972798665364,"t":"interior design, accounting, music, law enforcement, you name it. But what would","x":0.14595236347656226},{"h":0.018895348053517669,"t":"the founders of these two institutions have thought of a course called 'Arson for Profit?","x":0.14814814755055106,"w":0.78189300537109374,"c":1,"y":0.25145348875788265},{"t":"I kid you not: we have it on the books. Any undergraduates who have met the academic","h":0.021399528314705041,"y":0.26952160203508391,"w":0.79236862182617196,"c":1,"x":0.14599984283804654},{"t":"requirements can sign up for the course in our program in 'fire science.","w":0.64636118570963541,"c":1,"y":0.2881923849976129,"x":0.14593059219085244,"h":0.022778521156985088},{"x":0.14804072825872197,"h":0.02167131313867654,"c":1,"t":"Naturally, the course is intended for prospective arson investigators, who can learn all","w":0.76769454956054695,"y":0.31775072339165167},{"y":0.33716136625540627,"x":0.14609054347377839,"c":1,"h":0.018943284509881364,"w":0.77777776082356775,"t":"the tricks of the trade for detecting whether a fire was deliberately set, discovering who"},{"x":0.1480543369297512,"t":"did it, and establishing a chain of evidence for effective prosecution in a court of law.","y":0.35592670668013138,"h":0.022286494853780203,"w":0.76355290730794267,"c":1},{"y":0.37632508870200221,"c":1,"w":0.77777776082356764,"t":"But wouldn't this also be the perfect course for prospective arsonists to sign up for? My","h":0.019140164899882128,"x":0.15020576970487828},{"y":0.39455650429997835,"w":0.76352828979492204,"x":0.14805954677012959,"t":"point is not to criticize academic programs in fire science: they are highly welcome as","h":0.021173990516977215,"c":1},{"w":0.78823745727539063,"c":1,"x":0.14804070032230754,"h":0.022334288652148149,"t":"part of the increasing professionalization of this and many other occupations. However,","y":0.41290010202548866},{"w":0.72016459147135414,"t":"it's not unknown for a firefighter to torch a building. This example suggests how","y":0.43459302364479679,"h":0.018895348053517669,"x":0.14814815683384525,"c":1},{"t":"dishonest and illegal behavior, with the help of higher education, can creep into every","y":0.4523607451628946,"w":0.76966435750325513,"h":0.020438900825132,"c":1,"x":0.14808785486124076},{"h":0.021688575879423966,"c":1,"x":0.14788461426719512,"t":"aspect of public and business life.","y":0.47137291417763505,"w":0.3049768320719401},{"h":0.021754061515817158,"x":0.14804770653986907,"w":0.75946177164713535,"t":"I realized this anew when I was invited to speak before a class in marketing, which is","c":1,"y":0.50012794968870056},{"x":0.1502057634203057,"c":1,"t":"another of our degree programs. The regular instructor is a colleague who appreciates","h":0.018907332448431458,"w":0.76337448120117191,"y":0.52179034157530901},{"t":"the kind of ethical perspective I can bring as a philosopher. There are endless ways","x":0.1502057586252773,"y":0.53916372152348269,"w":0.73662551879882809,"c":1,"h":0.018975812779438939},{"y":0.55795476613297768,"w":0.72449590047200518,"h":0.02122052285921161,"c":1,"t":"I could have approached this assignment, but 1 took my cue from the title of the","x":0.15009361538023294},{"c":1,"h":0.021043752753411638,"w":0.76558639526367189,"t":"course: 'Principles of Marketing'. It made me think to ask the students, 'Is marketing","y":0.57722462904144523,"x":0.15011401387497111},{"c":1,"w":0.790321756998698,"h":0.022757016868276803,"t":"principled:ẾAfter all, a subject matter can have principles in the sense of being codified,","x":0.15007878515503573,"y":0.59501763742402425},{"c":1,"x":0.15009926720939176,"h":0.021971309423727492,"y":0.61525380321918544,"t":"having rules, as with football or chess, without being principled in the sense of being","w":0.76153879801432289},{"w":0.74706268310546886,"h":0.020793878849600156,"c":1,"t":"ethical. Many of the students immediately assumed that the answer to my question","y":0.63505111864417829,"x":0.15013169127008222},{"h":0.020740664047402935,"y":0.654265819962355,"c":1,"t":"about marketing principles was obvious: no. Just look at the ways in which everything","x":0.15012508403516117,"w":0.77381256103515605},{"h":0.022099909428572873,"c":1,"x":0.15213852605576675,"t":"under the sun has been marketed; obviously it need not be done in a principled","y":0.67291183287549672,"w":0.71221074422200525},{"c":1,"t":"(=ethical) fashion.","y":0.69379299452156984,"w":0.16922720591227214,"x":0.14998955598424946,"h":0.018511666566379259},{"x":0.1377786503901543,"c":1,"t":"Is that obvious? I made the suggestion, which may sound downright crazy in light of","w":0.77801228841145842,"h":0.02337304779160565,"y":0.72088827361979824},{"x":0.15020576884928127,"y":0.74116607828196535,"t":"the evidence, that perhaps marketing is by definition principled. My inspiration for this","h":0.019140164899882239,"c":1,"w":0.78395060221354163},{"h":0.021162626178862776,"x":0.14808027485396338,"y":0.75948211670502896,"t":"judgement is the philosopher Immanuel Kant, who argued that any body of knowledge","w":0.79231389363606775,"c":1},{"h":0.018946708301773363,"w":0.40534978230794272,"c":1,"t":"consists of an end (or purpose) and a means.","x":0.15226338034808626,"y":0.7805232561972878},{"y":0.94476744168840554,"t":"24","w":0.028806584676106764,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"x":0.10493827134507418},{"w":0.20827172597249349,"x":0.39483721539984068,"t":"leltsresources.org","c":1,"h":0.01645441358586508,"y":0.96768258547277797}]}